# Docker integration before push and MR

> **Captured/Updated**: 2026-08-28  
> **Owner**: `@aea-devsecops-platform` with `@aea-senior-software-engineer`  
> **Traceability**: Issue #274, CI/CD Pre-Push SOP  

Before `git push` and opening or updating a merge request, run the **local
Docker integration tests for every component the change actually impacts**.
Do not treat unit tests as a substitute.

## Recipes (do not invent a stack)

Use this repo’s existing Compose files, runners, and `AEA_INTEGRATION=1`
gates — the same path as CI `platform-foundation-integration` and the edge
README runner.

| Impact | Local recipe |
|---|---|
| Platform DB / migrations / Postgres (including pgvector when that is the Compose or CI image) | `python platform/scripts/run_integration_tests.py` |
| Kafka / outbox / relay / consumer / backbone | Same platform runner (`AEA_INTEGRATION=1` discovers Kafka/backbone tests) |
| Edge / BFF / gateway / UI / HTTPS perimeter | `python edge/scripts/run_integration_tests.py` |

Docs-only, Cursor-rule, or research-note changes: no Docker integration.

## Scope and failures

- Scope to impacted components. Do not run the full matrix “just in case”.
- If Docker is unavailable, **do not push as if integrations passed**. Say
  they were skipped and wait, or use CI only if the user explicitly accepts
  that.
- On failure: fix on the same branch, re-run the impacted suite, then push.
